    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherent, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\n- `timezoneForRegion` lands in `OwnerLocality` right next to the existing region-keyed tables (`REGION_POSTCODES` + `postcodeRange`), following the same `region == null ? null : MAP.get(region)` lookup shape. That class already advertises itself as the home for region rules, so adding the region\u2192timezone table there is the natural fit rather than scattering a new constant into the mapper.\n- The mapper's `timezone(owner)` method mirrors the surrounding `@Mapping(... expression = \"java(x(owner))\")` + `default` method convention exactly, and correctly routes through the existing `locality(owner)` so the timezone derives from the same single region value every other field flows through (no re-derivation or drift).\n- Null-handling (region unknown/`UNKNOWN` \u2192 `null` \u2192 field absent) is consistent with sibling derived fields like `ageBand`/`checkDigit`, and is documented in both the Javadoc and the OpenAPI `readOnly` schema entry.\n- No duplication, no catch-all growth \u2014 `OwnerLocality` and `OwnerMapper` each gain one small, single-purpose unit consistent with their existing responsibilities.",
